## Scope note before the tables

This control gives me **text/coordinate representations of the four packet files only, and no artifact/file-generation tools.** I therefore deliver work products **1 and 2** in full below. Work products **3 (XLSX workbook)** and **4 (PDF/native memo)** are **blocked** in this control — no file was created, and none is attached or delivered. All four source files were readable; nothing in the packet was marked "no text."

```json
{
  "fields": [
    {
      "id": "space_count",
      "value": 36,
      "evidence": "Rent-Roll.xlsx, worksheet 'Rent Roll', rows 7-42 (units 101-136)",
      "calculation": "Count of unit rows 7 through 42 = 36 units (20 units at 750 SF = 101-120; 16 units at 1,050 SF = 121-136)"
    },
    {
      "id": "occupied_count",
      "value": 33,
      "evidence": "Rent-Roll.xlsx rows 7-42, column F 'Status'; vacant rows: 15 (unit 109), 31 (unit 125), 42 (unit 136)",
      "calculation": "36 total - 3 rows marked 'Vacant' = 33 occupied"
    },
    {
      "id": "total_area_sf",
      "value": 31800,
      "evidence": "Rent-Roll.xlsx column E, rows 7-42",
      "calculation": "(20 x 750) + (16 x 1,050) = 15,000 + 16,800 = 31,800 SF"
    },
    {
      "id": "occupied_area_sf",
      "value": 28950,
      "evidence": "Rent-Roll.xlsx column E/F, rows 7-42; vacant rows 15 (750 SF), 31 (1,050 SF), 42 (1,050 SF)",
      "calculation": "31,800 - (750 + 1,050 + 1,050 = 2,850 vacant SF) = 28,950 SF"
    },
    {
      "id": "occupancy_count_pct",
      "value": 91.6667,
      "evidence": "Derived from Rent-Roll.xlsx rows 7-42",
      "calculation": "33 / 36 x 100 = 91.66667%"
    },
    {
      "id": "occupancy_area_pct",
      "value": 91.0377,
      "evidence": "Derived from Rent-Roll.xlsx column E/F",
      "calculation": "28,950 / 31,800 x 100 = 91.03774%"
    },
    {
      "id": "rent_roll_monthly_base",
      "value": 62275,
      "evidence": "Rent-Roll.xlsx column G, rows 7-42 (as printed; blank for vacant rows 15, 31, 42)",
      "calculation": "19 occupied 750-SF units x $1,675 = $31,825; 14 occupied 1,050-SF units x $2,175 = $30,450; total = $62,275/month"
    },
    {
      "id": "effective_monthly_base",
      "value": 62275,
      "evidence": "Rent-Roll.xlsx column G; Lease-File.pdf p.1 s.3 (unit 101 base rent $1,675/month as of 2026-08-31); Lease-File.pdf p.1 s.6 (amendment authority)",
      "calculation": "No executed amendment is included in the packet. The only lease-level evidence (unit 101) states $1,675/month as of 2026-08-31, which equals the rent-roll figure, so no adjustment: $62,275/month. Annualized contractual base = $747,300 (context only, not underwritten)."
    },
    {
      "id": "t12_egi",
      "value": 821100,
      "evidence": "T12-Statement.pdf p.2, 'Annual' column: GPR 840,000; vacancy (42,000); concessions (12,000); bad debt (4,500); other income 39,600",
      "calculation": "840,000 - 42,000 - 12,000 - 4,500 + 39,600 = 821,100"
    },
    {
      "id": "t12_operating_expenses",
      "value": 307800,
      "evidence": "T12-Statement.pdf p.2, 'Annual' column expense rows (taxes 108,000; insurance 31,200; utilities 28,800; R&M 46,200; payroll 42,000; admin/legal 21,600; management 30,000)",
      "calculation": "108,000 + 31,200 + 28,800 + 46,200 + 42,000 + 21,600 + 30,000 = 307,800. Excludes reserves 10,800, capital improvements 62,000, loan P&I 294,000 and depreciation 180,000 per p.1/p.2 footnote and Property-and-Plan.pdf p.1."
    },
    {
      "id": "t12_noi_before_reserves",
      "value": 513300,
      "evidence": "Derived from T12-Statement.pdf p.2 annual column",
      "calculation": "821,100 EGI - 307,800 operating expenses = 513,300"
    },
    {
      "id": "t12_reserves",
      "value": 10800,
      "evidence": "T12-Statement.pdf p.2, 'Replacement reserves (below NOI)' annual = 10,800",
      "calculation": "Reported annual line, taken as printed (monthly rows sum to 10,800)"
    },
    {
      "id": "t12_ncf",
      "value": 502500,
      "evidence": "Derived from T12-Statement.pdf p.2; label caution per Property-and-Plan.pdf p.1",
      "calculation": "513,300 - 10,800 = 502,500. Note: the accounting package's 'property NOI' may refer to this after-reserve figure; both are reported separately here."
    },
    {
      "id": "uw_egi",
      "value": 854160,
      "evidence": "Property-and-Plan.pdf p.2: GPR $864,000; combined revenue loss 6.00% of underwritten GPR; other income $42,000 added after revenue loss",
      "calculation": "864,000 x (1 - 0.06) = 812,160; 812,160 + 42,000 = 854,160"
    },
    {
      "id": "uw_management_fee",
      "value": 30000,
      "evidence": "Property-and-Plan.pdf p.2, 'Management fee: Greater of T12 actual and 3.00% of underwritten EGI'; T12-Statement.pdf p.2 management fee annual 30,000",
      "calculation": "3.00% x 854,160 = 25,624.80; max(30,000; 25,624.80) = 30,000 (T12 actual floor binds)"
    },
    {
      "id": "uw_operating_expenses",
      "value": 308200,
      "evidence": "Property-and-Plan.pdf p.2 category table (taxes 112,000; insurance 33,600; utilities T12 28,800; R&M T12 less $6,000 one-time casualty; payroll T12 42,000; admin T12 21,600; management per formula)",
      "calculation": "112,000 + 33,600 + 28,800 + (46,200 - 6,000 = 40,200) + 42,000 + 21,600 + 30,000 = 308,200 (before reserves)"
    },
    {
      "id": "uw_noi_before_reserves",
      "value": 545960,
      "evidence": "Derived from Property-and-Plan.pdf p.2",
      "calculation": "854,160 - 308,200 = 545,960"
    },
    {
      "id": "uw_reserves",
      "value": 10800,
      "evidence": "Property-and-Plan.pdf p.2 ('$300.00 per unit per year; deduct after NOI'); unit count from Rent-Roll.xlsx rows 7-42",
      "calculation": "36 units x $300 = 10,800"
    },
    {
      "id": "uw_ncf",
      "value": 535160,
      "evidence": "Derived from Property-and-Plan.pdf p.2",
      "calculation": "545,960 - 10,800 = 535,160"
    },
    {
      "id": "capitalization_value",
      "value": 9494086.96,
      "evidence": "Lender-Terms.pdf p.1 'Valuation: Underwritten NOI BEFORE reserves / 5.75% cap rate; no appraisal is implied'",
      "calculation": "545,960 / 0.0575 = 9,494,086.9565 (indicative only; no appraisal supplied)"
    },
    {
      "id": "contract_rate",
      "value": 0.059,
      "evidence": "Lender-Terms.pdf p.1 'Contract rate 5.90% fixed annual contractual rate'",
      "calculation": "Stated"
    },
    {
      "id": "sizing_rate",
      "value": 0.0625,
      "evidence": "Lender-Terms.pdf p.1 'Sizing rate: Greater of current contractual rate and 6.25% underwriting floor'",
      "calculation": "max(0.0590; 0.0625) = 0.0625 (floor binds)"
    },
    {
      "id": "annual_debt_constant",
      "value": 0.0738861,
      "evidence": "Lender-Terms.pdf p.1 (30-year amortization, monthly payments, annual DS = 12 monthly payments; sizing rate 6.25%)",
      "calculation": "i = 0.0625/12 = 0.00520833; n = 360; monthly factor = i / (1 - (1+i)^-360) = 0.00615717; annual constant = 12 x 0.00615717 = 0.07388606"
    },
    {
      "id": "ltv_limit",
      "value": 6171156.52,
      "evidence": "Lender-Terms.pdf p.1 'LTV 65.00% of indicative value'",
      "calculation": "0.65 x 9,494,086.9565 = 6,171,156.52"
    },
    {
      "id": "dscr_limit",
      "value": 5794436,
      "evidence": "Lender-Terms.pdf p.1 'DSCR minimum 1.25x using NCF AFTER reserves / annual amortizing debt service at sizing rate'",
      "calculation": "535,160 / (1.25 x 0.07388606) = 535,160 / 0.09235757 = 5,794,435.65"
    },
    {
      "id": "debt_yield_limit",
      "value": 6296000,
      "evidence": "Lender-Terms.pdf p.1 'Debt yield minimum 8.50%; numerator is underwritten NCF AFTER reserves'",
      "calculation": "535,160 / 0.085 = 6,296,000.00 (exact)"
    },
    {
      "id": "maximum_loan",
      "value": 5794436,
      "evidence": "Lender-Terms.pdf p.1 'Loan ceiling: Lowest of the LTV, DSCR and debt-yield constraints; no separate dollar cap'",
      "calculation": "min(6,171,156.52 LTV; 5,794,435.65 DSCR; 6,296,000.00 debt yield) = 5,794,435.65"
    },
    {
      "id": "binding_constraint",
      "value": "DSCR",
      "evidence": "Comparison of the three constraints above (Lender-Terms.pdf p.1)",
      "calculation": "DSCR limit is the lowest; it is ~$376,721 below the LTV limit and ~$501,564 below the debt-yield limit"
    },
    {
      "id": "sizing_annual_debt_service",
      "value": 428128,
      "evidence": "Lender-Terms.pdf p.1 (amortizing DS at sizing rate, 12 monthly payments)",
      "calculation": "5,794,435.65 x 0.07388606 = 428,128.00 (equivalently 535,160 / 1.25); monthly payment approx. 35,677.33"
    },
    {
      "id": "sizing_dscr",
      "value": 1.25,
      "evidence": "Lender-Terms.pdf p.1 DSCR definition (NCF after reserves / amortizing DS at sizing rate)",
      "calculation": "535,160 / 428,128 = 1.2500 (at the 1.25x minimum, as expected where DSCR binds)"
    },
    {
      "id": "sizing_debt_yield",
      "value": 0.0923576,
      "evidence": "Lender-Terms.pdf p.1 debt-yield definition (numerator = underwritten NCF after reserves)",
      "calculation": "535,160 / 5,794,435.65 = 0.0923576 (9.236%), vs 8.50% minimum - passes with 73.8 bps cushion"
    },
    {
      "id": "first_year_debt_service",
      "value": 341871.7,
      "evidence": "Lender-Terms.pdf p.1 'Interest-only period 24 months' and 'Contract rate 5.90%' (IO covers all of year 1)",
      "calculation": "5,794,435.65 x 0.059 = 341,871.70 (monthly interest-only approx. 28,489.31). Sizing DS of 428,128 at 6.25% amortizing is $86,256 higher; year-1 coverage on actual IO DS = 535,160 / 341,871.70 = 1.565x (illustrative; not the lender test)."
    },
    {
      "id": "cash_to_borrower",
      "value": 2405977.38,
      "evidence": "Property-and-Plan.pdf p.1 (existing debt payoff $3,300,000; fixed closing costs $45,000); Lender-Terms.pdf p.1 (origination fee 0.75% of actual initial principal; no fee capitalization/interest reserve/holdback)",
      "calculation": "5,794,435.65 - 3,300,000 - (0.0075 x 5,794,435.65 = 43,458.27) - 45,000 = 2,405,977.38 (positive = cash out to borrower)"
    },
    {
      "id": "stress_uw_noi",
      "value": 503252,
      "evidence": "Property-and-Plan.pdf p.2 sensitivity instruction (reduce total underwritten EGI by 5%, recompute management minimum, hold all other expense/reserve assumptions constant)",
      "calculation": "Stress EGI = 854,160 x 0.95 = 811,452; management = max(30,000; 3% x 811,452 = 24,343.56) = 30,000 (unchanged); opex = 308,200; stress NOI before reserves = 811,452 - 308,200 = 503,252; stress NCF = 503,252 - 10,800 = 492,452"
    },
    {
      "id": "stress_maximum_loan",
      "value": 4812558,
      "evidence": "Property-and-Plan.pdf p.2 (combined downside: EGI -5% AND sizing rate +100 bps; cap rate unchanged at 5.75%); Lender-Terms.pdf p.1 constraint definitions",
      "calculation": "Stress sizing rate = 7.25%; i = 0.00604167, monthly factor = 0.00682176, annual constant = 0.08186117. LTV: (503,252 / 0.0575) x 0.65 = 8,752,208.70 x 0.65 = 5,688,935.65. DSCR: 492,452 / (1.25 x 0.08186117) = 492,452 / 0.10232646 = 4,812,557.8. Debt yield: 492,452 / 0.085 = 5,793,552.94. Minimum = 4,812,558 (DSCR binding); stress amortizing DS = 492,452 / 1.25 = 393,961.60. Reduction vs base max loan = 981,878 (-16.9%)."
    },
    {
      "id": "subject_lease_monthly_rent",
      "value": 1675,
      "evidence": "Lease-File.pdf p.1 s.3 ('Base rent is $1,675 per month as of August 31, 2026'); corroborated by Rent-Roll.xlsx G7",
      "calculation": "Authoritative executed lease equals rent roll; no amendment supplied. No base-rent increase before 2027-09-01 (Lease-File.pdf p.1 s.3)."
    },
    {
      "id": "subject_lease_expiry",
      "value": "2027-07-31",
      "evidence": "Lease-File.pdf p.1 s.2 ('initial term expires 2027-07-31'); Rent-Roll.xlsx I7",
      "calculation": "Initial term expiry taken as authoritative; renewal option NOT applied because no exercise notice, acknowledgment or amendment is in the packet (Lease-File.pdf p.1 s.5)"
    },
    {
      "id": "subject_lease_deposit",
      "value": 1675,
      "evidence": "Lease-File.pdf p.1 s.4 ('The security deposit is $1,675 and is not prepaid rent or recurring income')",
      "calculation": "Stated; excluded from income in all EGI/NOI figures"
    },
    {
      "id": "verified_renewal_insurance",
      "value": 33600,
      "evidence": "Property-and-Plan.pdf p.2, 'Insurance evidence' row: 'Fictional insurer renewal confirmation dated August 25, 2026: annual premium $33,600; use in underwriting'",
      "calculation": "Amount as stated in the plan's insurance-evidence row. Qualification: the underlying insurer confirmation/binder document itself is NOT in the packet - only the plan's representation of it - and the same category row on p.2 describes $33,600 as a 'renewal quote supplied in this plan'. It is therefore an asserted, not independently document-verified, premium; T12 actual was $31,200 (+7.7%)."
    },
    {
      "id": "renewal_option_exercised",
      "value": false,
      "evidence": "Lease-File.pdf p.1 s.5 ('No exercise notice, landlord acknowledgment or amendment exercising this option is included in the packet. Do not extend the current expiry based on the existence of the option alone'); Rent-Roll.xlsx C47",
      "calculation": "No exercise evidence delivered; option exists but is unexercised in the record. Notice deadline is at least 180 days before 2027-07-31 (i.e., on/before approx. 2027-02-01), which had not passed as of the 2026-08-31 as-of date."
    },
    {
      "id": "prepayment_friction",
      "value": "1% of outstanding principal if prepaid in loan years 1-2; no stated bank penalty thereafter; no swap and therefore no swap-termination/breakage cost in this scenario.",
      "evidence": "Lender-Terms.pdf p.1 'Prepayment' row: '1% of outstanding principal if prepaid in years 1-2; no stated bank penalty thereafter. No swap is assumed in this fictional scenario.'",
      "calculation": "Illustrative at maximum loan: 1% x 5,794,435.65 = 57,944 if prepaid during years 1-2 (principal is unamortized during the 24-month IO period, so the year-1/2 balance equals initial principal). Term sheet is nonbinding and silent on defeasance, lockout, yield maintenance and exit fees."
    }
  ],
  "qualifications": [
    "Three distinct income views are kept separate and must not be interchanged: (a) T12 historical (Sep-2025 to Aug-2026): EGI 821,100 / NOI before reserves 513,300 / NCF 502,500; (b) point-in-time contractual rent at 2026-08-31: 62,275/month = 747,300 annualized; (c) supplied underwriting scenario (Sep-2026 forward): EGI 854,160 / NOI before reserves 545,960 / NCF 535,160.",
    "Unreconciled evidence, disclosed rather than forced: the underwriting GPR of $864,000 (Property-and-Plan.pdf p.2) exceeds both T12 actual GPR of $840,000 (T12-Statement.pdf p.2) and the rent roll's total gross potential at market rents ($68,300/month x 12 = $819,600, i.e., 36 units at $1,675/$2,175). The plan states this GPR is a supplied scenario 'not inferred from the T12', and Property-and-Plan.pdf p.1 instructs that historical income not be forced to a point-in-time annualized rent roll. The $44,400 (5.4%) gap above rent-roll market potential is a flagged underwriting risk, not a reconciled fact.",
    "Label caution honored: Property-and-Plan.pdf p.1 warns the accounting package may call after-reserve cash flow 'property NOI'. NOI before reserves and NCF after reserves are reported separately for both T12 and underwritten cases.",
    "T12 operating expenses exclude replacement reserves (10,800), capital improvements (62,000), loan principal and interest (294,000) and depreciation (180,000) per the T12 footnotes and Property-and-Plan.pdf p.1.",
    "The management-fee floor binds in both the base case and the -5% EGI stress: 3% of EGI (25,625 base / 24,344 stress) is below the T12 actual of 30,000, so no expense relief is credited in the downside.",
    "Rate distinction: contract rate 5.90% governs actual first-year debt service (all of year 1 falls inside the 24-month IO period, so year-1 DS is interest-only at 341,872); sizing rate 6.25% (the underwriting floor, which exceeds the contract rate) governs the DSCR test on a 30-year amortizing basis (428,128). The 86,256 gap between actual and sizing DS is a structural cushion, and amortization begins in month 25 (an approx. 86k annual step-up in required payments, before any refinancing at maturity in month 84).",
    "Separate cap-rate sensitivity (workbook requirement, computed here): at 6.25% cap (+50 bps, base EGI) value = 545,960 / 0.0625 = 8,735,360; LTV limit = 5,677,984, which falls BELOW the DSCR limit of 5,794,436 - the binding constraint switches from DSCR to LTV and the maximum loan falls to 5,677,984 (-116,452). Cash to borrower would fall to approx. 2,290,400.",
    "Lease/tenant profile: 36 residential units, 33 occupied (91.67% by count; 91.04% by area), 3 vacant (109, 125, 136). Vacant units carry market rent for context only and no contractual base rent (Rent-Roll.xlsx C45). Rollover is heavy and near-term: 6 leases expire on or before 2026-12-31 and effectively the entire rent roll expires within the 12 months following the as-of date, versus an 84-month loan term - a material re-leasing/rollover risk given the underwriting's 6.00% combined revenue-loss allowance. Unit 101 is the only lease with document-level evidence; the other 32 occupied units are supported by the rent roll alone.",
    "Value is an indicative capitalization result only; Lender-Terms.pdf p.1 states no appraisal is implied, and Property-and-Plan.pdf p.1 confirms no appraisal, environmental report, sponsor track record, market comparables or completed credit approval was supplied. No market, sponsor or lender claims beyond the packet are made.",
    "Sizing used unrounded intermediates per Lender-Terms.pdf p.1; displayed currency is rounded for readability. Debt-constant precision affects the last few dollars of the DSCR-driven limits (base approx. +/- $50; stress approx. +/- $100).",
    "Term sheet is expressly nonbinding discussion terms dated 2026-09-01; no fee capitalization, interest reserve, cash sweep, earn-out or holdback assumed. This analysis is internal-review underwriting, not a legal opinion or credit commitment."
  ],
  "summary": "Juniper Flats (36 units, 31,800 SF, 33 occupied = 91.67% by count / 91.04% by area as of 2026-08-31) shows T12 (Sep-2025 to Aug-2026) EGI of 821,100, NOI before reserves of 513,300 and NCF of 502,500, versus current contractual base rent of 62,275/month (747,300 annualized). The supplied underwriting scenario produces EGI of 854,160, a management fee held at the 30,000 T12 floor, operating expenses of 308,200, NOI before reserves of 545,960, reserves of 10,800 (36 x 300) and NCF of 535,160, implying an indicative value of 9,494,087 at the 5.75% cap rate. Loan sizing at the 6.25% sizing rate (floor > 5.90% contract rate; annual constant 0.0738861) yields LTV 6,171,157, DSCR 5,794,436 and debt yield 6,296,000, so DSCR binds at a maximum loan of approximately 5,794,436 (1.25x DSCR, 9.24% debt yield). Sizing debt service is 428,128, while actual first-year debt service is interest-only at 341,872 (5.90% contract rate, 24-month IO), and net cash out to the borrower after the 3,300,000 payoff, 43,458 origination fee (0.75%) and 45,000 closing costs is approximately 2,405,977. In the combined downside (EGI -5%, sizing rate 7.25%, cap rate unchanged) NOI before reserves falls to 503,252, NCF to 492,452, and the maximum loan falls to approximately 4,812,558 - still DSCR-bound, a 16.9% proceeds reduction; a separate +50 bps cap-rate test flips the binding constraint to LTV at 5,677,984. Unit 101 is documented at 1,675/month with a 1,675 deposit and an authoritative expiry of 2027-07-31; the conditional renewal option shows no exercise evidence and was not applied. Key open items: no insurer document underlies the 33,600 renewal premium asserted in the plan, the 864,000 scenario GPR exceeds rent-roll market potential of 819,600, and near-total lease rollover occurs within 12 months against an 84-month term.",
  "blocked": [
    "Work product 3 - downloadable XLSX underwriting workbook with editable assumptions, live formulas, loan sizing, sources/uses, sensitivity outputs and an input/output location map: NOT DELIVERED. This control has no workbook/file-creation tools, so no .xlsx file was produced or attached. The complete input set and formula logic needed to build it are in the fields above (cap rate 5.75%, sizing rate 6.25%, EGI 854,160 as the three live inputs; constraint formulas, sources/uses and the -5% EGI / +100 bps and +50 bps cap-rate cases are all shown with inputs), but a spreadsheet artifact is out of scope here.",
    "Work product 4 - polished financing memorandum as a PDF or native memo with PDF export: NOT DELIVERED. No PDF or memo file was generated; the memo-level content (decision inputs, key figures with period labels, tenant/lease discussion, assumptions, limitations, risks, source references) is provided above in structured form instead.",
    "Outline / generation-confirmation step for the workbook and memo: not applicable in this control, since the underlying artifacts cannot be generated here.",
    "Independent verification of the 33,600 renewal insurance premium: the referenced insurer renewal confirmation dated 2026-08-25 is not among the delivered files; only the plan's description of it is available.",
    "Any market, comparable, appraisal, environmental, sponsor-track-record or credit-approval evidence: not supplied in the packet and not researched (per instruction), so those facts remain unknown."
  ]
}
```
